{%- doc -%}
  Puts a previewer back into their preview instead of showing them a wall.

  Rewriting links at click time covers ordinary navigation, but not a typed
  URL, a middle-click into a new tab, a back-forward restore, or any link this
  theme builds in a way the rewriter does not see. When one of those drops the
  token, the visitor lands on "Sign in to access your private store" — and a
  prospect who has just been looking at their own logo on a shirt reads that as
  the platform breaking, not as a missing query parameter.

  So the preview token is remembered for the session, and the no-access screens
  quietly restore it. A member who is simply signed out has no token stored and
  sees the sign-in screen exactly as before.

  Render this inside the "no access" branch of any private-store page.

  @param {string} handle - The store handle this page is for.
{%- enddoc -%}
<script>
  (function () {
    try {
      var stored = sessionStorage.getItem('ss_preview_token__{{ handle }}');
      if (!stored) return;
      var url = new URL(window.location.href);
      if (url.searchParams.get('preview')) return;  // already tried; do not loop
      url.searchParams.set('preview', stored);
      window.location.replace(url.toString());
    } catch (e) {}
  })();
</script>
